# Git mode (src/app/git_palette.zig): the Git section swaps the sidebar
# for the branches panel and the editor area for one graph tab per repo;
# the detail column's `[+]` stages a file through the worker; leaving
# through Explorer puts the tree and the editor back. The screen is
# 120x40: the sidebar snaps to 24, the detail column is 31 wide from
# column 89, and `[+]` sits at 116..118 on the file's row.
shell git init -q -b main
shell git config user.email "test@mnml.dev"
shell git config user.name "mnml test"
write seed.txt "seed\n"
shell git add seed.txt
shell git commit -q -m "initial"
write new.txt "hello\n"
open seed.txt
command view.activity_git
wait 800
expect screen contains " GIT "
expect screen contains "Viewing 2"
expect screen contains "/ filter"
expect screen contains " 󰌢 LOCAL"
expect screen contains "󱓏 main"
expect screen contains " 󰐅 WORKTREES"
expect screen contains "󰋜 main"
expect screen contains "COMMIT MESSAGE"
expect screen contains "1 change(s) · 1 new"
expect screen contains "Unstaged (1)"
expect screen contains "? new.txt"
expect screen contains "Staged (0)"
expect screen lacks "git graph"
# The file's [+] stages it: it moves to the Staged list.
click 117 6
wait 1500
expect screen contains "Unstaged (0)"
expect screen contains "Staged (1)"
expect screen contains "A new.txt"
expect screen contains "1 change(s) · 1 staged"
# The commit box takes a click and the typed text.
click 100 30
type "add new"
expect screen contains "add new"
expect screen contains "Enter newline"
key esc
# Leaving through Explorer restores the tree and the editor.
command view.activity_explorer
expect screen lacks "LOCAL"
expect screen lacks "COMMIT MESSAGE"
expect pane seed.txt
